      "writtenOn": "2015-11-10T22:46:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you need an implementation details comment right here. The comment should explain why you treat KeyStore \u003d\u003d null and !\u003d null so differently. You could add the comment right at the start of the method, or split it into the two branches, one for ks \u003d\u003d null and the other for after that block.\n\nFor example: When a TrustManager is initialized with a null KeyStore it must use its own default trust configuration. We use the application\u0027s trust config. When a TrustManager is initialized with a non-null KeyStore, it must base its trust decisions on the contents of that KeyStore. We don\u0027t want to deal with this and thus delegate that to a TrustManagerFactory from another provider.",
      "revId": "0542bdaa673633e1b218777075c75d9d8d4aa867",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
